00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:14,500
I won't be easily seen!

259
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:15,840
You can't go back!

260
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:18,668
That area is surely
filled with dust by now!

261
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:21,280
Ahhhh! There it is! Quick!

262
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:23,077
We must turn around at once!

263
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:25,737
A warrior spirit will guide
him through any obstacle,

264
00:14:25,820 --> 00:14:28,040
be it deadly gas or a blazing fire!

265
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:29,570
Vumanosuke!

266
00:14:29,653 --> 00:14:30,757
A warrior spirit or not?

267
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:31,899
That's impossible!

268
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:35,360
Well, this happened.

269
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:37,320
What was he thinking?

270
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:39,870
Luffy!

271
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:42,060
Hey, Nani!

272
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:43,968
Great, you're here already!

273
00:14:44,580 --> 00:14:47,437
Oh no, what happened
to Brownie? Is he okay?

274
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:51,637
yeah he should be fine
well actually I don't know

275
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:58,077
there see I

276
00:14:58,160 --> 00:15:00,477
told you don't

277
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:02,057
worry about the kids they'll

278
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:05,177
be fine my friends are on
their way to help and they

279
00:15:05,260 --> 00:15:09,220
always keep their word just
worry about yourself for now

280
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:14,790
Move it!

281
00:15:14,873 --> 00:15:17,017
I gotta see Nami again,
and you're holding me up!

282
00:15:17,100 --> 00:15:18,017
I don't see Chopper.

283
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:19,041
That's not good.

284
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:23,971
He slowed down earlier to get first aid
to that girl, and that's all I know.

285
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:34,580
I need this. It's huge.

286
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:36,994
Yeah, that's the idea.

287
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:38,657
They use this cart to haul S .A .D.

288
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:39,570
Get it?

289
00:15:39,653 --> 00:15:44,760
That means we can use it to halt
people and this whole lab is done for.

290
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:45,882
There's no time

291
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,480
Straw Hats

292
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:52,640
Traffy, Smoky, where'd you come from?

293
00:15:53,940 --> 00:15:54,770
Smoky

294
00:15:55,860 --> 00:15:57,300
Hey, look guys.

295
00:15:57,860 --> 00:15:58,937
He made it.

296
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:00,037
Thank goodness.

297
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:03,377
I was so scared.

298
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:04,977
Smoky, hold on.

299
00:16:05,060 --> 00:16:08,137
I'm reporting when I'm
done crying. What's that?

300
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:09,380
Shut your traps.

301
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:13,520
It's fine.

302
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:17,140
Hey, Straw Hat, where did Caesar go?

303
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:19,900
Oh, see that hole there?

304
00:16:20,060 --> 00:16:21,766
I blew him straight that way.

305
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:23,332
Door kind of got busted.

306
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:24,370
What?

307
00:16:24,453 --> 00:16:28,420
No, the plan was to
kidnap him. Why? He sucks.

308
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:30,297
Come on, we should just leave him behind.

309
00:16:30,380 --> 00:16:32,537
That is not what we both agreed on.

310
00:16:32,620 --> 00:16:36,320
If he escapes from here the
plan is ruined. I don't care.

311
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:37,874
I'm done good riddance

312
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:42,017
The point of having a plan is
to follow through with it I

313
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:44,417
should have known better than
to trust you with anything.

314
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:46,120
We got to get him back now

315
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:53,360
A short time ago, a strange sight could
be seen in the skies near Punk Hazard.

316
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:57,078
Little did the Straw Hats
know what they were in for?

317
00:16:57,400 --> 00:17:00,217
Once this mission is over then I'm done.

318
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:02,240
I'll kill him. You hear me?

319
00:17:02,620 --> 00:17:03,740
with my own hands.

320
00:17:03,900 --> 00:17:05,600
I won't forgive you, Joker.

321
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:09,500
So cruel, it wasn't enough
to blow up my dear fiancé.

322
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:12,037
You had to burn his whole town to ash too.

323
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:13,600
He did you no wrong.

324
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:16,320
How many men must you kill?

325
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:19,900
Every time I get engaged, blow
my darling to little bits.

326
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:21,960
Eight men and eight towns.

327
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:23,720
Enough is enough.

328
00:17:24,100 --> 00:17:26,340
Why won't he let me be happy? Me?

329
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:28,897
That's just how he shows his love.

330
00:17:28,980 --> 00:17:30,197
He's just protective.

331
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:33,557
He thinks of you like his little
sister, that sort of thing.

332
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:37,464
Him blowing up a town or two is
just a sign of how much he cares.

333
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:42,297
Besides, this only happens because you
haven't learned how to say no to those chums.

334
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:43,909
And what made him a chump?

335
00:17:44,020 --> 00:17:45,400
He said he needed me.

336
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:47,422
How could I turn my back on him?

337
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:51,720
It's love at first sight.

338
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:53,080
Will you marry me?

339
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:54,650
What?

340
00:18:00,660 --> 00:18:05,017
Look here's the deal, just cuz
someone asks—you don't gotta say yes.

341
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:09,357
You don't need 50 newspaper
subscriptions; no one does,

342
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:13,357
and stop lending out all of your money—we're
wasting it on crap you don't need,

343
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:14,270
Chouchou.

344
00:18:14,353 --> 00:18:16,197
How much debt do you got?

345
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:17,537
Why do you care?

346
00:18:17,620 --> 00:18:19,677
It's 98 million—that's all.

347
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:22,077
This is none of your
business, if you're...

348
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:27,340
business if you're Fine.

349
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:28,840
Lend me some.

350
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:29,980
Say two mil.

351
00:18:31,020 --> 00:18:31,850
What?

352
00:18:31,933 --> 00:18:33,300
He needs me.

353
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:38,660
Um, can I pay you later?

354
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:40,110
Mm-hmm.

355
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:42,652
When we're done, I needed to go gambling.

356
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:44,320
Okay, then.

357
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:48,148
Once we finish our mission, I'll
take out a new loan for you.

358
00:18:50,520 --> 00:18:52,620
Joker needed me to carry this out.

359
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:54,237
After that, it's over.

360
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:55,849
Bastard's as good as dead.

361
00:18:57,620 --> 00:18:58,600
That's it!

362
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,800
Honk Hazard, straight ahead!

363
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:05,137
I can't see anything.

364
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:07,691
Caesar's gas is covering the whole island.

365
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,660
If I shoot it, will that help any?

366
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:13,580
No way! Hop off!

367
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:15,717
I've got this, no problem.

368
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:16,740
I'll be quick!

369
00:19:26,980 --> 00:19:28,680
It's typhoon time!

370
00:19:28,980 --> 00:19:29,880
Let's go!

371
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:35,840
Storm God! Matagamuro!

372
00:19:42,920 --> 00:19:44,360
They'll be here soon.

373
00:19:44,780 --> 00:19:46,960
Caesar, Monet, and Vergo, too.

374
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:52,894
I sure can't wait to spend
all your money at the casino!

375
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:04,837
Did one of the tanks just explode?

376
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:07,840
No, something went flying into the ship!

377
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:13,320
Not something, someone.

378
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:24,237
Joker, Mrs.

379
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:25,617
Buffalo, I got you!

380
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:26,759
That's a bad news.

381
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:28,110
What's up?

382
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:30,100
Well, you see, we made it.

383
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:32,957
But it looks like something
went down before we got here.

384
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:36,160
We just saw Master Caesar,
but he was all busted up.

385
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:38,897
He went flying out of the
lab and into the tanker.

386
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:40,921
Like someone kicked his ass hard.

387
00:20:41,180 --> 00:20:42,240
Is that so?

388
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:50,657
I don't care what state he's in.

389
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:52,152
Grab Caesar immediately.

390
00:20:52,240 --> 00:20:54,887
Get out of there and
bring him to dress Rosa.

391
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:57,240
But Monet and Vanko!

392
00:20:57,700 --> 00:20:59,220
Just do what he says.

393
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:01,029
There must be some reason.

394
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:03,140
Okay! So long!

395
00:21:10,300 --> 00:21:11,940
Bunch of damn rookies.

396
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:13,297
Blow up the lab.

397
00:21:13,380 --> 00:21:14,792
What the hell do I care?

398
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,220
It'll take more than that to beat me.

399
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:19,700
All that matters is Caesar.

400
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:23,920
As long as I have him, I can
make all the S .A .D. I need.

401
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,277
Wait, there's someone down on the
deck, but that can't be right.

402
00:21:31,360 --> 00:21:33,520
No way, not with all that gas.

403
00:21:33,780 --> 00:21:36,780
You sure it's not just some
dead body or something?

404
00:21:41,560 --> 00:21:42,620
It's a robot!

405
00:21:46,860 --> 00:21:49,380
Man, that's what messed up looking bird.
